  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Fair weather this weekend will give way to more\nunsettled weather into early next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure builds in through the weekend, with drier weather\nand cooler temperatures returning to the forecast area. High \ntemperatures each day may only lift into the 70s, and skies \ncould remain mostly sunny on Saturday. By Sunday, cloud cover \nmay begin to increase once more ahead of the next approaching \nlow pressure system, though there is the possibility this system\ncould slow upon approach, delaying the onset of mostly cloudy \nskies to early next week.\n\nThe next low pressure system to cross the area early next week \nwill be in the form of a cold front which brings another round \nof rain and chance for thunderstorms. Current trends suggest \nshowers will remain scattered along the boundary as they move \nthrough as there will be a lack of deep moisture support, but if\nthe trough deepens more and reaches further into the Gulf, \nthere could be more numerous showers and storms due to the \nsynoptic forcing of the cold front. The latest ECMWF and CMC\nguidance suggest the potential for a triple point low along the\ncoast as this system enters our area, which could better enhance\nforcing along the coast and support higher rainfall totals\nthrough the Downeast region. Meanwhile, the GFS keeps the\nfeature as an ordinary cold front pushing through the forecast\narea. The GFS-AI model does parallel the coastal low thinking,\nalong with other AI guidance and the end of the RRFS run, so the\npotential exists for better wetting rains near the coast, much\nas the NBM has with at least a quarter of an inch of widespread\nrainfall Downeast.",
